      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: Practice Questions\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "Kreyszig is limited in terms of practice questions and some of you have asked for alternatives. \n",
        "\n",
        "Two books you can use to circumvent that are:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Dennis G. Zill's Advanced Engineering Mathematics\n",
        "- Dean G. Duffy's Advanced Engineering Mathematics\n",
        "\n",
        "Zill's book in particular has a lot of practice problems. \n",
        "\n",
        "Notwithstanding, you can use `julia` to create your own problems. All you need is a way to create a matrix. \n",
        "\n",
        "The following creates a 4x3 matrix with numbers randomly filled from 1 to 10. "
      ],
      "id": "9aa1ea0a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "mat = rand(1:10, 4, 3)"
      ],
      "id": "b0bac412",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "You can make changes to it and generate as many questions as you want. "
      ],
      "id": "06c38ff9"
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
